  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vijay Sharma vs Food Corporation Of India on 18 July, 2024 Author: Sanjeev Narula Bench: Sanjeev Narula $~87 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + W.P.(C) 9748/2024 Vijay Sharma Th ve Food Corporation Of India Through: Mr. Manoj, Standing Food Corporation o Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Sanjeev Narula Or % 18.07.2024 Cm Appl. 39967/2024 (Exemption) 1. Exemption is granted, subject to all just exceptions.",
    "facts": "The dispute in the present writ petition arises from the Agreement dated 25th July, 2018, entered into by the parties for the work of \"Demolition and Reconstruction of 20 nos. of Residential Flats in Sector-27, Noida\". The results of Testing Report so submitted by the appointed agency indicates that the work was not executed according to specifications and also strength of the structure was not as per requirement of scheduled items resulting various losses to the Corporation. And",
    "arguments": "Mr. Ankur Mahindro, Counsel for Petitioner assails the aforenoted communication, to the extent that it directs debarment of the Petitioner from participating in any future tenders of the Respondent, for a period of 5 years from the date of issuance of the said letter."
  },
